IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`
IMPORT `coa10-period`
IMPORT `coa10-filing`

-- coa10-tests-filing.l4: tests for coa10-filing.l4 (ss 441, 443A to 447). Every expected value was written down from the
-- text of the section (line numbers in ukpga-2006-46.txt) before the module was run; none is copied from its output.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The three-valued helpers (Kleene): a JUST FALSE or JUST TRUE decides; otherwise NOTHING.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `s 441 both are true` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 441 both are true` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 441 both are true` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 441 both are true` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 441 both are true` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 441 both are true` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 441 both are true` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 441 either is true` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 441 either is true` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 441 either is true` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 441 either is true` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 441 either is true` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 441 either is true` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 441 either is true` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 441 the opposite of` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 441 the opposite of` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 441 the opposite of` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Which section applies (ss 441(1), 443A(1), 444(1) and (6), 444A(1) and (5), 445(1) and (7), 446(1) and (5), 447(1))
-- The fields of `s 441 facts about the company`, in order: the text relied on; s 384A; s 384B; s 381; s 384; s 415A; s 465; s 385(3) unquoted; s 385(2) quoted.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- a micro-entity (so also subject to the small companies regime and unquoted), second text
`s 441 fixture micro-entity second text` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 second text in the file`, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
-- the same company read under the first text
`s 441 fixture micro-entity first text` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 first text in the file`, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
-- a small company that is not a micro-entity and is entitled to the directors' report exemption
`s 441 fixture small company second text` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 second text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
`s 441 fixture small company first text` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 first text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
-- a company that would be small but for being a member of an ineligible group (second text only describes it)
`s 441 fixture ineligible group second text` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 second text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
`s 441 fixture ineligible group first text` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 first text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
-- a company that would be small but for an ineligible group and is entitled to the directors' report exemption, read under the first text (the only company 444A reaches that 444 does not)
`s 441 fixture ineligible group with the directors' report exemption first text` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 first text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
-- a medium-sized unquoted company
`s 441 fixture medium-sized company` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 second text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
-- a large unquoted company
`s 441 fixture large unquoted company` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 first text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE
-- a quoted company
`s 441 fixture quoted company` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 second text in the file`, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE
-- nothing known
`s 441 fixture unknown company` MEANS `s 441 facts about the company` OF `s 441 second text in the file`, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

-- Section 443A: the description is micro-entity (or would be but for an ineligible group); no exclusion.
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) section 443A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity second text` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) section 443A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity first text` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) section 443A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company second text` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) section 443A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture unknown company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 444, second text (6): not a company within 443A.
#ASSERT `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity second text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company second text` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group second text` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture medium-sized company` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture unknown company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 444, first text: no exclusion, so a micro-entity subject to the regime is within it too.
#ASSERT `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity first text` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group first text` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 444A (5): not a company within section 444.
#ASSERT `s 444A(1) section 444A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company second text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 444A(1) section 444A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company first text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 444A(1) section 444A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture medium-sized company` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 444A(1) section 444A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture unknown company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 445 (7).
#ASSERT `s 445(1) section 445 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture medium-sized company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (7): "This section does not apply to companies within section 444": a small company is within 444, so the text says no whatever its size. (First written as NOTHING; corrected on re-reading s 445(7), which speaks to companies within 444 and not only to those it describes.)
#ASSERT `s 445(1) section 445 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company second text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 445(1) section 445 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company first text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 445(1) section 445 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture unknown company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 446 (5): unquoted, and not within 443A (second text) or 444, 444A (first text) or 445.
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture large unquoted company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture medium-sized company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity second text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity first text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company first text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture quoted company` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture unknown company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 447.
#ASSERT `s 447(1) section 447 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture quoted company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 447(1) section 447 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture large unquoted company` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 447(1) section 447 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture unknown company` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 441(1): the section the accounts and reports are required under.
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity second text` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 443A`
-- The first text lets 443A and 444 both reach a micro-entity and the text does not say which governs: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture micro-entity first text` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company second text` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 444`
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture small company first text` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 444`
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group second text` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 444`
-- In the first text the ineligible-group company is not described by section 444 (only "subject to the small companies regime"): no section describes it as small, but it is unquoted: section 446 is described; its exclusions find no section it is within.
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group first text` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 446`
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture medium-sized company` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 445`
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture large unquoted company` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 446`
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture quoted company` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 447`
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture unknown company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 444A reaches a company that is entitled to the directors' report exemption without being within 444 (first text: 444 describes only "subject to the small companies regime").
#ASSERT `s 444A(1) section 444A applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group with the directors' report exemption first text` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (7) of 445 and (5) of 446, first text, exclude a company within 444A.
#ASSERT `s 445(1) section 445 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group with the directors' report exemption first text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group with the directors' report exemption first text` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` `s 441 fixture ineligible group with the directors' report exemption first text` EQUALS JUST `s 441 section 444A`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What each section requires, document by document.
-- The fields of `s 441 facts about what is delivered`, in order: exempt from audit and advantage taken; the profit and loss account is delivered; abridged; there is a separate corporate governance statement.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`s 441 delivery plain` MEANS `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 441 delivery exempt from audit` MEANS `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 441 delivery profit and loss account delivered` MEANS `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 441 delivery profit and loss account delivered and exempt from audit` MEANS `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 441 delivery abridged` MEANS `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s 441 delivery with a separate corporate governance statement` MEANS `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- Section 443A (lines 5938-5942).
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 annual accounts` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 directors' report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors may deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 auditor's report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 auditor's report` `s 441 delivery exempt from audit` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the section does not require it`
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 balance sheet` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 strategic report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Section 444, first text (lines 5949-5957).
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 balance sheet` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 profit and loss account` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors may deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 directors' report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors may deliver it`
-- (2): the auditor's report is required only where the profit and loss account is delivered, and not where exempt from audit.
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 auditor's report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the section does not require it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 auditor's report` `s 441 delivery profit and loss account delivered` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 auditor's report` `s 441 delivery profit and loss account delivered and exempt from audit` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the section does not require it`
-- (2A): the consent statement where the accounts are abridged.
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 statement that all the members have consented to the abridgement` `s 441 delivery abridged` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 statement that all the members have consented to the abridgement` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the section does not require it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 annual accounts` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the first text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 strategic report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Section 444, second text (lines 5983-5987).
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the second text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 annual accounts` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the second text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 directors' report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the second text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 auditor's report` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the second text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 auditor's report` `s 441 delivery exempt from audit` EQUALS JUST `s 441 the section does not require it`
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the second text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 balance sheet` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 444(1) what the second text of section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `s 441 profit and loss account` `s 441 delivery plain` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Section 444 with the text chosen by the caller.
